abstract: >-
  An open, machine-readable dataset of complexity pairs: computational problems for which two or more
  provably correct algorithms of different asymptotic cost are recorded. Every entry carries an explicit
  verification level that is enforced by the included validator: V1 for implementations that agree with
  each other and an independent oracle, and V2 for measured growth (wall-clock time or exact operation
  counts) that fits the claimed cost and rejects declared rival costs. Results, refutations, corrections
  and null results are documented in a research log, with machine-recorded evidence for every validation run.
